PMFHL/PMTHL with the R5900 pipeline-1 registers (LO1/HI1), in the runtime macros and the recompiler.
Why: PS2_PMFHL_*(hi, lo) read only LO0/HI0 and packed them in the wrong order. Metrowerks __muldi3 (Jackass
0x1B0E38: mult, multu1, madd, pmfhl.lw, pcpyud) then returned 0 for small products, so strtol("505") gave 5,
the DISK.MAP loader stopped after 5 entries, later files read sector 0 and the start-up resource load failed.
Semantics from the EE Core Instruction Set manual / PCSX2 MMI.cpp. Test: tests/pmfhl_muldi3_test.cpp in
jackass-ps2-recomp (12 failures before, 0 after). Needs a ps2_recomp rebuild and a regenerate.
Origin: this project (jackass-ps2-recomp), 2026-10-27; Killzone recomp patch 0010 fixed PMFHL.SH the same way.

diff --git a/runtime/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp b/runtime/ps2xRecomp/src/lib/mmi_translation_helpers.cpp
